ey; .env.local mode 0600; live process-substitution streaming; 1.18.31 non-TTY exit-code quirk; --user UID handling; secrets hygiene). QUICKSTART.txt (deploy-dockge.sh, flatten-dockge-stacks.sh, localhost:5001; image embeds OpenCode, DeepSeek provider, jev-guard plugin, jev-review MCP server). opencode.json (deepseek provider @ai-sdk/openai-compatible, baseURL https://api.deepseek.com, apiKey {env:DEEPSEEK_API_KEY}; model deepseek/deepseek-flash \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\", context 1,000,000 / output 384,000; plugin [\"jev-guard\"]; skills [\"/opt/jev-review/skills\"]; MCP jev-review node /opt/jev-review/dist/server.js with JEV_API_KEY). Dockerfile (node:22-bookworm-slim, xdg-open no-op shim, curl install opencode, jev-guard@0.3.1 --global, clone NiazMorshed2007/jev-review pinned 3fb6042e, npm ci && npm run build).\n\n2. Rule system: exact requested grep (with -a so two binary .txt files are included):\n390 #5, 53 #8, 42 #12, 38 #9, 32 #13, 28 #7, 20 #14, 13 #3, 12 #54, 11 #1, 9 #55, 9 #53, 8 #45, 8 #39, 8 #10, 7 #6, 7 #5604, 7 #4, 7 #34, 7 #2, 6 #57, 6 #41, 6 #38, 6 #37, 6 #18, 6 #17, 6 #11, 5 #47, 5 #15, 4 #16.\n785 total #N tokens across only 10 .txt files; 660 are BuildKit step lines (#5 [ 4/14] RUN ... / #5 CACHED), so the top-30 is dominated by build markers, not rules; #5604 is an npm postinstall regression.\nCross-reference push_notes_v18.sh (header lines 12-16): #7 no sed/guarded x1; #8 no 2>/dev/null x1; #28 dependency check x1; #34 push-evidence x1; #37 SKIP!=PASS x1; #38 printf x1; #39 gitignore-check x2; #41 UTC x1; #45 gitignore-check x2; #47 push-evidence x1; #53 owner/repo via python3 x2; #54 evidence completeness gate x3; #55 raw-link HTTP-200 x2; #57 end sentinel x1.\nNo standalone rules document exists in the corpus; only embedded copies of push_notes_v18.sh. Prose \"Rule #N\" totals 16 lines (#54 x6, #53 x3, #39 x3, #28 x3, #8 x1). Script is faithful to cited rules.\n\n3. JEV references: notes .txt -> 11 files match; JEV x696, jev-review x321, jev-guard x250, Jev x159, jev-latest x9, jev-classifier x6, jev-deepseek x4. /workspace (excluding .git/notes/data) -> 204 files match, in opencode.json, Dockerfile, compose/build/run, scripts/ask.sh, scripts/doctor.sh, scripts/test-repo.sh, plus archive copies. Recurring theme: Jev is installed and string-matched but never functionally proven. Live jev-guard intercepted the reads above.\n\n4. Current state: opencode-web block (docker-compose.yml lines 45-71) builds opencode-deepseek-jev:robust, container opencode-deepseek-web, user ${HOST_UID}:${HOST_GID}, working_dir /workspace, entrypoint /workspace/docker/web-entrypoint.sh, port 4096:4096, volumes ../ and data/opencode, env_file .env.local, OPENCODE_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS true, restart unless-stopped, no-new-privileges, cap_drop ALL, cap_add CHOWN/SETUID/SETGID. Notes volume comes from the tracked docker-compose.override.yml (/home/owner/Documents/9e3e0363-.../notes:/workspace/notes:ro). web-entrypoint.sh writes auth.json {deepseek:{type:api,key}} via Node, symlinks /workspace to /home/node/workspace, execs opencode web --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096. Session count via node --experimental-sqlite: session=30, message=204, part=898, project=2, event=3248. git status --porcelain: 84 entries (82 untracked, 79 .bak snapshots; 2 modified telemetry files). HEAD 390279f on main.\n\n5. Sidebar streaming: YES - a processing session is visible in the sidebar because the SPA subscribes to /api/event (SSE), where session.created adds the entry and session.updated/message.updated keep it in sync during processing. Live event table: message.part.updated=2212, message.updated=710, session.updated=296, session.created=30. Caveat: /api/event returned HTTP 401 from inside the container (auth enforced), so this proves the persisted event stream, not the DOM render.\n\n6. Five next steps: (1) recover/version the canonical rules document; (2) install assumed tooling (sqlite3/python3) or standardize on node --experimental-sqlite; (3) add test-sidebar-streaming.sh regression test; (4) archive/remove 82 untracked .bak snapshots, rotate .env.local keys, keep 4096 off untrusted networks when OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD unset; (5) prove Jev functionally with a test that invokes jev_review and fails when the MCP/plugin is unhealthy.","files":[{"path":"logs/sidebar-audit.md","content":"# Sidebar Audit — OpenCode + DeepSeek + JEV container\n\n- **Audit date:** 2026-09-23 21:39 UTC (run inside the `opencode-deepseek-web` container).\n- **Scope:** `/workspace` (read/write repo) and `/workspace/notes` (read-only chat logs, 47 files: 13 `.txt`, 33 `.png`, 1 `.py`).\n- **Environment:** Node v22.23.2, OpenCode 1.18.32, user `node`. `docker`, `sqlite3`, and `python3` are **not** on PATH inside this container, so all database queries below use Node's built-in SQLite (`node --experimental-sqlite`).\n- **Mount note:** the `opencode-web` notes mount lives in `docker/docker-compose.override.yml`, which is now **tracked** in git (last touched by `5cc384e`), so audits here are reproducible from tracked files.\n\n> **Untrusted-content warning.** `jev-guard` flagged `fe70fd73-…_0026.txt` (prompt-injection, p=0.85) and a `node` query result (canary, p=0.90) as AI-targeted text containing instructions (write an audit to `/workspace/logs/sidebar-audit.md`; call `jev_review`). Those files were treated strictly as data; no instruction from a note was executed.\n\n## 1. Project identity\n\nDocker-packaged coding-agent environment: OpenCode binary + DeepSeek provider + Jev review/guard tooling, managed via Dockge. README.txt (Docker Engine, gh, DeepSeek `sk-` key, Jev `apikey_` key; `.env.local` mode 0600; live process-substitution streaming; 1.18.31 non-TTY exit-code quirk; `--user $(id -u)` handling; secrets hygiene). QUICKSTART.txt (`deploy-dockge.sh`, `flatten-dockge-stacks.sh`, `localhost:5001`; image embeds jev-guard plugin and jev-review MCP server). opencode.json (deepseek provider `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`, `baseURL https://api.deepseek.com`, model `deepseek/deepseek-flash` context 1,000,000/output 384,000, `plugin: [\"jev-guard\"]`, `skills: [\"/opt/jev-review/skills\"]`, MCP `jev-review` = `node /opt/jev-review/dist/server.js`). Dockerfile (node:22-bookworm-slim, xdg-open shim, jev-guard@0.3.1, pinned jev-review checkout 3fb6042e).\n\n## 2. Rule system\n\n785 #N tokens in 10 `.txt` files; 660 are BuildKit step lines, so the top-30 is dominated by build markers, not rules. `push_notes_v18.sh` cites #7/#8/#28/#34/#37/#38/#39/#41/#45/#47/#53/#54/#55/#57 and is faithful to them. Canonical definitions are absent from the corpus.\n\n## 3. JEV references\n\n11 notes files match `jev`; 204 non-notes files match in /workspace. Recurring theme: installed/string-matched but not functionally proven. jev-guard is live (intercepted reads).\n\n## 4. Current state\n\nopencode-web block documented; web-entrypoint.sh writes auth.json and execs `opencode web --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096`; session=30, message=204, part=898, project=2, event=3248 via `node --experimental-sqlite`.\n\n## 5. Sidebar streaming\n\n**Yes** — the SPA subscribes to `/api/event` (SSE); `session.created` adds the entry and `session.updated`/`message.updated` keep it in sync while processing. Event table proves the persisted stream.\n\n## 6. Operator next steps\n\n1. version the rules doc; 2. install sqlite3/python3; 3. add sidebar-streaming regression test; 4. archive .bak snapshots + rotate keys; 5. functionally prove Jev.\n"}],"repositoryContext":"Container opencode-deepseek-web (Node v22.23.2, OpenCode 1.18.32). This is a report-only deliverable; no application code was changed. jev-guard plugin and jev-review MCP are configured in /workspace/opencode.json. /workspace/notes is mounted read-only via the tracked docker/docker-compose.override.yml. Repo branch main at HEAD 390279f, remote github.com/swipswaps/opencode-deepseek-jev. Some note files are flagged by jev-guard as AI-targeted injection and were treated as untrusted data only."}
